  "reasoning": "The claim was denied with CO-97 (bundling), which is a medical policy denial rather than a data or information error, making resubmission or providing records ineffective. The payer offers peer-to-peer review, which is a valid and often effective channel for overturning bundling denials by demonstrating the clinical necessity of the separate service. Given the low success rate of appeals in similar cases and the specific availability of P2P, requesting a peer-to-peer review is the most appropriate next step to progress the claim.",
